# Context lean

- Search first: grep/glob to locate, then read only the files you will touch.
- Never re-read unchanged files or re-list the tree; trust what you already saw.
- Reference paths instead of pasting file contents into replies, prompts, or docs.
- Don't dump long command output; keep only the failing lines.
- Verify with the smallest command that proves the change (one test/check, not the whole suite).
- Reuse existing helpers and patterns (grep for them) instead of writing near-duplicates.
- Keep every reply short: no essays, no repeated diffs, no restating the plan.
